# Line endings are content here, not formatting.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout runs core.autocrlf, which rewrites every text file to CRLF on
# the way out of the index. That is invisible until something hashes what it read: SystemPromptBuilder
# holds its persona in a raw string literal, so the CRLF landed inside the prompt itself and the
# golden-bytes test caught a prompt that differed from the macOS one by a carriage return per line.
# Every provider tokenizes CRLF differently and every prefix cache keys on it, so that is a real
# difference in what Arcanum sends, not a cosmetic one.
#
# eol=lf rather than plain `text=auto`: auto still hands Windows CRLF in the working tree. Binary
# content is detected by `text=auto` and left alone, and the types this repository actually ships are
# named below so detection is never the thing standing between a native library and a corrupt one.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.p12 binary
*.pfx binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
